section__
  @title "T326 - ACT5 - Dragonstone Blood Price at first light"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/05-act5-war-council/frame-326.jpg"

  "At first light on Dragonstone, sulfur and sea mist roll across black rock while emissaries lay out terms beneath a banner that snaps like a whip. You are offered dragon support for one critical strike in exchange for hostages, future tribute, and public recognition of precedence in the coming settlement. Davos reads the fine print like a sailor reading storm clouds. Tyrion smiles like he has seen this bargain before and survived it once.

Your captains are already brittle. Desertions rose after the census, and men trust spectacle more than policy when fear is high. A visible dragon commitment could restore morale in a day. It could also tell every ally that command now rests on fire instead of law.

You can bind this pact in strict public limits and keep a legal spine. Or you can arrange a private understanding that gives you immediate force with fewer witnesses and more future debt."

  choice__
    @target "T327 - ACT5 - Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Sign a limited dragon accord in open assembly, define targets by law, and accept scrutiny from every ally."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T328 - ACT5 - The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 7)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Negotiate a shadow pact for immediate dragon pressure, conceal true concessions, and secure compliance through fear."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T327 - ACT5 - Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/05-act5-war-council/frame-327.jpg"

  "Night fog sits low over Blackwater Bay, thick with tar smoke and fish rot. Merchant captains wait at anchor with sealed holds and higher prices every hour. They will move grain, lamp oil, and arrow stock where you ask, but only if someone guarantees losses from raids, seizures, or sudden policy reversals. In wartime language, that means one thing: who pays when promises fail.

Davos pushes for a transparent maritime charter with fixed escort duties and posted penalties. Tyrion suggests flexible private guarantees tied to names, secrets, and future favors, arguing that formal commitments are easy for enemies to exploit. Meanwhile, your camp stores are already trending short and the next week of campaigning depends on waterborne supply.

You can stabilize trade through lawful contract and visible accountability. Or you can run it through private coercion and hidden obligations. Both routes move cargo. Only one leaves a paper trail you can defend in front of hostile lords."

  choice__
    @target "T328 - ACT5 - The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Enact a public bay charter with audited rates and escort law, taking slower deals for durable legitimacy."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T329 - ACT5 - The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Guarantee shipments through private debt notes and blackmail collateral, binding captains to your hidden terms."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T328 - ACT5 - The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/05-act5-war-council/frame-328.jpg"

  "The Dreadfort galleries stink of wet fur, lamp smoke, and old blood that never quite leaves the stone. Border captains crowd the hall with mud still on their boots, demanding a final muster order before they commit to open ground. Bolton envoys insist they are loyal while refusing to release route maps unless compensated. Stark scouts call that extortion disguised as caution.

Raven traffic has become a weapon. Half your orders arrive with altered phrasing and missing seals, then return to you as proof of your own inconsistency. If this border force leaves fragmented, your next engagement starts with mismatched timing and empty flanks. If you enforce unity too violently, you risk sparking the very betrayal you are trying to prevent.

You need one answer now: visible, lawful alignment that costs flexibility, or covert pressure that secures immediate obedience and deepens long-term fear. The banners above you barely move in the draft, like men holding their breath."

  choice__
    @target "T329 - ACT5 - The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Confirm the border muster in open record, standardize command signals, and absorb slower deployment for cohesion."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T330 - ACT5 - Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 5)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Threaten key border lords in private, secure obedience through hostages and rumor, and move before dissent organizes."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T329 - ACT5 - The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/05-act5-war-council/frame-329.jpg"

  "At the Eyrie, thin mountain air tastes of candle wax and frost while heralds wait for your ruling. House Valehart now sits at the hinge of three theaters, and your ruling here will redirect riders, stores, and hostages before dawn. Tyrion Lannister tests your posture in public while Davos Seaworth studies your pauses for weakness, and every scribe in the room is already drafting competing versions of your intent.

Command coherence is now a resource. If orders split by faction, your grain routes collapse first and your battle plans fail second.

You must decide whether Valehart leads through visible law or covert coercion. Both routes can keep the alliance moving tonight, and both create enemies you will meet again before this act closes."

  choice__
